          "year": 2012,
          "date_decided": "2012-12-19",
          "holding": "The court held that caseworkers who failed to investigate abuse referrals and closed a foster child's case before he was starved and beaten to death were not entitled to qualified immunity, because the special relationship with a child in state custody and his right to reasonable safety were clearly established.",
