          "year": 2016,
          "date_decided": "2016-08-31",
          "holding": "The court held that disputed material facts about whether and how CYFD placed children at a private residential ranch precluded summary judgment on whether the Tort Claims Act building waiver in Section 41-4-6(A) permitted suit, and it reversed and remanded.",
          "relevance": "Litigation like this is the practical substitute in New Mexico for a published fatality or serious-injury review of a licensed facility.",
          "quote": "We conclude that questions of material fact preclude summary judgment on the issue of whether the TCA's building waiver applies to permit Plaintiffs' suit",
          "url": "https://www.courtlistener.com/opinion/4331998/quevedo-ex-rel-bevan-v-new-mexico-children-youth-families-department/",
